meta {
  name: Search
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/ai-search
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "prompt": "Toon alle openstaande orders voor Cone Lighting deze maand"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Happy-path AI search - a concrete, selective search prompt. See
  Backend/src/Luna/BusinessLogic/AiSearchBE.cls for the full orchestration
  (Gemini stage 1 -> whitelist validation -> existing entity BE dispatch ->
  aggregation -> Gemini stage 2 summary + anti-hallucination check).

  Response is always 200 with one of three resultType values:
  "results" | "no_results" | "clarification" - see the class header /
  Backend/README.md "AI Search" section for the full shape of each.

  Note: if GEMINI_API_KEY is not configured on the PASOE agent (see
  Backend/README.md), stage 1 fails and this same request instead returns
  502 with {"error": {"message": "De AI-zoekfunctie is momenteel niet
  beschikbaar. Probeer het later opnieuw.", "code": 502}} - confirmed live
  in the dev environment this feature was built against. Loosen the
  `res.status: eq 200` assertion above (or add a GEMINI_API_KEY to the
  Local environment) if running against an instance without a configured
  key.
}

